pairing check: windows whose paired [DIAG] tick lies > 60 ms from the [SLAW] close: 0

== A. Retransmits against the window minimum, per arm (LATE windows; 'retx' = the [DIAG] retx= delta in the same tick > 0) ==
  base = share of windows with a retransmit; low10 = share among the row's lowest-decile tmin windows; crit = crfollow's floor criterion
  (tmin < row median tp50 - 4 ms): its share of windows and their retx share; dT = median tmin of no-retx windows - of retx windows (ms);
  g8 = share of 8-window groups (2 s) whose lowest window carries a retransmit (no association: = base); ancf = [SLAW]'s anchor-bind count
  (windows where m-hat > l-hat + b-hat0+, of those with the law's inputs; the bind fraction of R6.2's min(m-hat, .)) at the last LATE window
  m = LATE median m-hat; tmin = median native tmin; G8 = median 8-window group minimum (ms)
