== D. The gates for each floor candidate (r67's screens, r68's uniqueness and R-sign gates), one leg, on the c3 arms' medians over rows (ms) ==
   margin(W) = target(W) - statistic(W), target = F + A; A = decision 8's form at Bulk (g = 1, q = 0.10) with the cell's native floor numbers:
   A = S_F + q*F-hat, S_F = the floor arm's median window (p50 - tmin), F-hat = the floor arm's median tmin. For K5 the same S_F is a PLACEHOLDER
   (decision 8's spread mapped to the median is not logged), so K5's crossing W is not read; its signs and crossing count are.
   Gates: margin > 0 at the floor arm, < 0 at the control, exactly one sign change along W (R crosses 1 once).
   K1 R6.2 as the law would read on each arm: F = min(m, l + b0p) + b0p from that arm's own LATE medians; statistic tmin
   K2 a running brake: F = m + median over the arm's LATE windows of (tmin - m) (what any at-load brake reads); statistic tmin
   K3 candidate C at the floor's count: F = the floor arm's median tmin, fixed; statistic tmin
   K4 count-matched minimum: F = M0(n_W), the median group minimum of g = round(n_W / n_floor) pooled LATE floor windows; statistic tmin
   K5 count-free location: F = the floor arm's median window p50, fixed; A = S_F + q*F (placeholder S_F); statistic the window p50
